- order_status_events
- payment_records
- offers
- gallery_images
- contact_enquiries
- cookie_preferences where necessary

Use suitable foreign keys, indexes, constraints, timestamps and database types.

Order items must preserve the price and product details at the time the order was placed, so later menu changes do not change historical orders.

Security:
- Enable Supabase Row Level Security on exposed tables.
- Public visitors can read only published, available menu content and other intentionally public information.
- Customers can access only their own orders and personal information, subject to the selected guest-checkout design.
- Guest orders must use secure, unguessable order access tokens or another server-controlled access method.
- Never expose private customer records publicly.
- Only authorised staff can manage products, orders, settings, offers and analytics.
- Assign administrator roles securely; never let a visitor promote themselves to admin by editing their profile.
- Never expose Supabase service-role credentials or privileged keys in the browser.
- Validate sensitive operations on the server.
- Rate-limit public forms and order creation where supported.
- Add secure handling for errors and sensitive logs.

Include an `.env.example` containing variable names only, without real secrets, and document how to configure Supabase.

